problem_statement:
You are given a set of untyped JavaScript utility functions. Add appropriate TypeScript types to make them type-safe while preserving their original behavior.

Untyped implementation:

function calculateTotal(items) {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
}

function filterActive(users) {
  return users.filter(user => user.isActive);
}

function greet(name, age) {
  return `Hello, ${name}! You are ${age} years old.`;
}

function findUserById(users, id) {
  return users.find(user => user.id === id);
}

Add appropriate TypeScript types to:
1. The function parameters
2. The function return types
3. Any object properties referenced in the functions

Define appropriate interfaces or type aliases where needed. Use specific types (e.g., number instead of any) when the type is clear from the context. Keep the function logic unchanged—only add types.
